import Library.Numerics.Float64.Trig.TrigPi

/-!
The distance of a double from the nearest multiple of `π/2`.  For each exponent field `E` from
1022 to 2046, a certificate `(p, q)` with `gcd p q = 1` and `q ≥ 2 ^ 53` approximates
`β = 2 ^ (E - 1075) · invPi` modulo 1, and the kernel checks that
`1/q - 2 ^ 53 |β - p/q| > 2 ^ -62`.  For `0 < m < q`, `q` does not divide `m p`, so
`|m p/q - n| ≥ 1/q`, and `|m β - n| > 2 ^ -62` for every integer `n`.  Every double from 1/2 on
is `m · 2 ^ (E - 1075)` with `m < 2 ^ 53`, and `invPi` lies within `2 ^ -1216` of `2/π`, so its
quotient by `π/2` lies more than `2 ^ -63` from every integer.  The certificates are convergents
of the continued fractions of the binades' `β`, computed offline; the smallest bound among them,
`2 ^ -61.54`, belongs to `E = 1872`, the binade of `6381956970095103 · 2 ^ 797`.
-/

